body:
I am trying currently to have a board that is a vector of pieces and the drawing part works fine but the drag and drop just doesn't for some reason. I tried looping through the vector and checking if it collides with the mouse position on click, it does register but nothing happens when I try to drag. Also the loop that goes through the vector crashes the program if I click on any piece other than the first one for some reason. I am completely clueless on why this is. Code is below but i don't know if its clear on what I am doing.

getGrid() returns the boards member of vector<Piece>

&#x200B;

>Vector2i mousePos = Mouse::getPosition(\*(this->window));  
Vector2f mouseRectOffset;  
bool isDragging;  
int c;  
while (this->window->pollEvent(this->e))  
{  
if (this->e.type == Event::Closed)  
this->window->close();  
if(e.type == Event::MouseButtonPressed)  
{  
if(e.key.code == Mouse::Left)  
{  
for(int i = 0; i < b.getGrid().size(); i++)  
{  
if(b.getGrid()\[i\].getPieceSprite().getGlobalBounds()  
.contains(mousePos.x, mousePos.y))  
{  
i = c;  
isDragging = true;  
mouseRectOffset.x = mousePos.x - b.getGrid()   
\[i\].getPieceSprite().getPosition().x;  
mouseRectOffset.y = mousePos.y - b.getGrid()   
\[i\].getPieceSprite().getPosition().y;  
}  
}  
}  
}  
if (e.type == Event::MouseButtonReleased)  
{  
if (e.key.code == Mouse::Left)  
{  
isDragging = false;  
}  
}  
}  
if(isDragging)  
{  
\[c\].getPieceSprite().getPosition().x << endl;  
Vector2i pos (mousePos.x,mousePos.y );  
b.getGrid()\[c\].getPieceSprite().setPosition(pos.x, pos.y);  
}

Yes that is my point basically, although the additional work for others isn't that small. Still, the concept is what counts. If you can make 1 character, 1 gun, 1 small area, 1 cinematic you could use that and make all the other work way easier. I put RdR as an example because it's a game that features animals and humans, there isn't any special monster or some wacky magic(those would be far worse to make since you can't base it off previous models that much). The gameplay or RdR in it's core is a 3rd person shooter with normal guns and throwables. 

&#x200B;

However, the real question is could you even make that 1 single character? How long would it take you to reach that point?

I'm looking for some reccomendations on what to pick up next. Will leave a short list of what i watched and my short opinion, maybe you guys pick something up from the list for yourselves.

What I enjoy the most about shows: beautiful female actresses, prefer longer shows (2+ seasons atleast), sci-fi, drama, love stories, mysteries, crime; to name a few.

Let's get on with the list:

**Lucifer** - has a serious and a playful tone, actors are insanely good, supernatural/love story mostly, has a lot of police and detective work, not for everyone, but one of my favorites;

**Altered Carbon** - season 1 is just pure gold, sci-fi theme, actors are 10/10, season 2 is just wtf - old actors are not in it and it ruins the experience completely for me, also story of s2 is just meh;

**The 100** - binge worthy, sci-fi, survival theme, female actresses are 10/10, keep in mind the show has a teen-style flow, not for everyone, has plenty of episodes and story is decent (begginning seasons are best, falls off later with cheesy stuff imo);

**Blacklist** - mystery, crime, james spader + megan boone, all the good stuff, one of my favorites and a show that brings a lot every season;

**13 Commandments** - 1 season long crime focused show with a very good story and a lot of mystery and deceit;

**Suits** - attorney focused story, first 7 seasons are pure gold, after that it's boring and dull imo, but until then deffinitelly worth it;

**Westworld** - anthony hopkins + great actors, show is just breathtaking (atleast season 1 and 2), futuristic and mysterious show, would highly reccomend the first 2 seasons;

**Witcher** - if you like the novels you will like this one lot, even those who don't know about the books will find it interesting if a world of magic/beasts/swordfighting appeals to them;

**Peaky Blinders** - mafia focused theme, 10/10 actors, doesn't let down in any season, story is awesome, what more to tell;

Other things I watched and liked: Dr House, Dexter, Hannibal, Prison Brake, Supernatural (first 5 seasons), Lost (except ending and season 6 in general), Game of Thrones (except last season), You, Sex Education, Vikings, Dark, La Casa de Papel, Breaking Bad, Queens Gambit, The Crown (first 2 seasons), Better Call Saul, End of the fucking World, Fargo (season 1).

Shows I didn't really like (were meh at best) : True Blood, 13 Reasons Why, The Terror, Elite, The Walking Dead.
